From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:26:05 +0200
Subject: dt-bindings: net: dsa: lantiq,gswip: describe the xRX500 switch
 interrupt

Each GSWIP-3.0 macro raises one shared interrupt, aggregating everything it
can report: the buffer manager, the parser and classification engine, the
MAC block, and the store and fetch DMA blocks.

Optional, because no driver takes it: this switch reaches the same state by
polling. It is a fact about the block either way.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/lantiq,gswip.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/lantiq,gswip.yaml
index a4bc851a74a4..4aedd6f51add 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/lantiq,gswip.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/lantiq,gswip.yaml
@@ -38,6 +38,13 @@ properties:
 
   dma-noncoherent: true
 
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The macro's aggregated interrupt, raised by the buffer manager, the
+      parser and classification engine, the MAC block and the store and
+      fetch DMA blocks.
+
   clocks:
     items:
       - description: switch core clock
@@ -320,6 +327,8 @@ examples:
     switch@1c000000 {
             compatible = "lantiq,xrx500-gswip";
             reg = <0x1c000000 0x4000>;
+            interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+            interrupts = <0 48 4>;
             clocks = <&cgu 22>, <&cgu 125>;
             clock-names = "freq", "gate";
             dsa,member = <0 0>;
